IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore): s 10 -- who may be a company's auditor. (ss 9 and 11 are shown repealed by Act 40 of 2018.)
--
-- Whether a person is an "accounting entity" is s 4(1)'s question (sg-definitions.l4: `s 4(1) "accounting entity" the person is an
-- accounting entity`); this module takes the answer as the input `the person is an accounting entity`, so that it imports the
-- core only. A seat builds that input from the four facts s 4(1) asks.

§ `Section 10(1): who may consent to be appointed, or act, as auditor`

DECLARE `s 10(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 10(1)(a) knowingly consent to be appointed as auditor for a company`
    `s 10(1)(b) knowingly act as an auditor for a company`
    `s 10(3) appoint an accounting entity as an auditor of a company without obtaining the accounting entity's prior consent`

-- src:2740 | 10.—(1) No person other than an accounting entity may —
-- src:2742 | (a) knowingly consent to be appointed as auditor for a
-- src:2743 | company; or
-- src:2745 | (b) knowingly act as an auditor for a company.
@ref s 10(1) (src:2740-2745)
GIVEN `the person is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) the person may consent to be appointed, or act, as auditor for a company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an accounting entity`) AND `the person acts knowingly`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person other than an accounting entity may (a) knowingly consent to be appointed as auditor for a company; or (b) knowingly act as an auditor for a company" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars a person who is not an accounting entity and who acts "knowingly"; it grants an accounting entity no permission, and says nothing of one who does not act knowingly

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule: derived from the flat negative (the N2 ruling of 2026-11-04), the party being any person who is not an accounting entity.
@ref s 10(1) (src:2740-2745)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 10(1) act`
`s 10(1) a person who is not an accounting entity must not knowingly consent to be appointed as auditor` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 10(1)(a) knowingly consent to be appointed as auditor for a company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "a person who is not an accounting entity knowingly consented to be appointed as auditor for a company"

@ref s 10(1) (src:2740-2745)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 10(1) act`
`s 10(1) a person who is not an accounting entity must not knowingly act as auditor` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 10(1)(b) knowingly act as an auditor for a company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "a person who is not an accounting entity knowingly acted as an auditor for a company"

§ `Section 10(2): what acting as auditor includes`

-- src:2749 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1)(b), a person acts as an auditor
-- src:2750 | for a company if the person prepares any report required by this Act to
-- src:2751 | be prepared by an auditor of the company.
@ref s 10(2) (src:2749-2751)
GIVEN `the person prepares a report required by this Act to be prepared by an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) the person acts as an auditor for the company` MEANS
    IF `the person prepares a report required by this Act to be prepared by an auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Without limiting subsection (1)(b), a person acts as an auditor for a company if ..." leaves other ways of acting as auditor open

§ `Section 10(3): appointing an accounting entity`

-- src:2755 | (3) No company or person may appoint an accounting entity as an
-- src:2756 | auditor of a company without obtaining the accounting entity’s prior
-- src:2757 | consent.
@ref s 10(3) (src:2755-2757)
GIVEN `the prior consent of the accounting entity has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3) the company or person may appoint the accounting entity as an auditor of the company` MEANS
    IF `the prior consent of the accounting entity has been obtained`
    THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No company or person may appoint ... without obtaining the accounting entity's prior consent" bars an appointment made without it, and grants no power to appoint where consent was obtained
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No company or person may appoint an accounting entity as an auditor of a company without obtaining the accounting entity's prior consent" (a flat negative)

@ref s 10(3) (src:2755-2757)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 10(1) act`
`s 10(3) no person may appoint an accounting entity as auditor without its prior consent` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 10(3) appoint an accounting entity as an auditor of a company without obtaining the accounting entity's prior consent`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "an accounting entity was appointed as an auditor of a company without its prior consent"

§ `Section 10(4): the form of the consent`

DECLARE `s 10(4) kind of accounting entity` IS ONE OF
    `s 10(4)(a) a public accountant`
    `s 10(4)(b) an accounting firm`
    `s 10(4)(b) an accounting limited liability partnership`
    `s 10(4)(c) an accounting corporation`

-- The paragraph names who must sign: the public accountant; at least one partner of the firm or limited liability partnership;
-- at least one director of the accounting corporation.
-- src:2761 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the consent —
-- src:2763 | (a) of a public accountant must be in writing signed by the
-- src:2764 | public accountant;
-- src:2766 | (b) of an accounting firm, or an accounting limited liability
-- src:2767 | partnership, must be in writing signed by at least
-- src:2768 | one partner of the firm or limited liability partnership; and
-- src:2773 | (c) of an accounting corporation must be in writing signed by
-- src:2774 | at least one director of the corporation.
@ref s 10(4) (src:2761-2774)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 10(4) kind of accounting entity`
      `the consent is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by at least one partner of the firm or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by at least one director of the accounting corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(4) the consent has the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the consent is in writing` AND (CONSIDER kind
                                        WHEN `s 10(4)(a) a public accountant` THEN `it is signed by the public accountant`
                                        WHEN `s 10(4)(b) an accounting firm` THEN `it is signed by at least one partner of the firm or limited liability partnership`
                                        WHEN `s 10(4)(b) an accounting limited liability partnership` THEN `it is signed by at least one partner of the firm or limited liability partnership`
                                        WHEN `s 10(4)(c) an accounting corporation` THEN `it is signed by at least one director of the accounting corporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the consent (a) of a public accountant must be in writing signed by the public accountant; (b) of an accounting firm, or an accounting limited liability partnership, must be in writing signed by at least one partner ...; and (c) of an accounting corporation must be in writing signed by at least one director" (a duty not met, the provision's own question)

@ref s 10(4) (src:2761-2774)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 10(4) kind of accounting entity`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 10(4) who must sign the consent` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 10(4)(a) a public accountant` THEN "the public accountant"
    WHEN `s 10(4)(b) an accounting firm` THEN "at least one partner of the firm"
    WHEN `s 10(4)(b) an accounting limited liability partnership` THEN "at least one partner of the limited liability partnership"
    WHEN `s 10(4)(c) an accounting corporation` THEN "at least one director of the corporation"

§ `Section 10(5) and (6): who is appointed when a firm or corporation is appointed in its own name`

-- src:2778 | (5) Where an accounting firm is appointed as auditor of the
-- src:2779 | company in the name of the accounting firm, the appointment takes
-- src:2780 | effect and operates as if the partners of the firm at the time of the
-- src:2781 | appointment, who are public accountants at that time, are appointed
-- src:2782 | as auditors of the company.
@ref s 10(5) (src:2778-2782)
GIVEN `the accounting firm was appointed as auditor of the company in the name of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a partner of the firm at the time of the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a public accountant at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the person is appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting firm` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the accounting firm was appointed as auditor of the company in the name of the firm`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accounting firm is appointed as auditor of the company in the name of the accounting firm, the appointment takes effect and operates as if ..." (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-S4 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF    `the person was a partner of the firm at the time of the appointment`
             AND `the person was a public accountant at that time`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says the appointment operates as if "the partners of the firm at the time of the appointment, who are public accountants at that time" are appointed, with no "only"; it says nothing of a partner admitted later or of a partner who is not then a public accountant (fork line F-S4 in NOTES.md)

-- src:2786 | (6) Where an accounting corporation is appointed as auditor of the
-- src:2787 | company in the name of the corporation, the appointment takes effect
-- src:2788 | and operates as if —
-- src:2790 | (a) the directors of the corporation who are practising as public
-- src:2791 | accountants in the corporation (whether directors at the
-- src:2792 | time the accounting corporation was appointed as auditor
-- src:2793 | or later); and
-- src:2795 | (b) the employees of the corporation who are practising as
-- src:2796 | public accountants in the corporation (whether employed
-- src:2797 | at the time the accounting corporation was appointed as
-- src:2798 | auditor or later),
-- src:2800 | are appointed as auditors of the company. [36/2014]
@ref s 10(6) (src:2786-2800)
GIVEN `the accounting corporation was appointed as auditor of the company in the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the corporation practising as a public accountant in the corporation, whether a director when the corporation was appointed or later` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of the corporation practising as a public accountant in the corporation, whether employed when the corporation was appointed or later` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(6) the person is appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting corporation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the accounting corporation was appointed as auditor of the company in the name of the corporation`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accounting corporation is appointed as auditor of the company in the name of the corporation, the appointment takes effect and operates as if ..." (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-S4 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF    `the person is a director of the corporation practising as a public accountant in the corporation, whether a director when the corporation was appointed or later`
             OR `the person is an employee of the corporation practising as a public accountant in the corporation, whether employed when the corporation was appointed or later`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the directors and employees practising as public accountants, with no "only"; it says nothing of any other person

-- The gap: s 4(1) makes an accounting limited liability partnership an accounting entity, and s 10(4)(b) treats it like a firm for consent,
-- but neither s 10(5) nor s 10(6) says which individuals are appointed when one is appointed in its own name.
-- src:2778 | (5) Where an accounting firm is appointed as auditor of the
-- src:2779 | company in the name of the accounting firm, the appointment takes
-- src:2780 | effect and operates as if the partners of the firm at the time of the
-- src:2781 | appointment, who are public accountants at that time, are appointed
-- src:2782 | as auditors of the company.
@ref s 10(5) (src:2778-2782)
GIVEN `the accounting limited liability partnership was appointed as auditor of the company in its own name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner of the limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) and (6) the person is appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting limited liability partnership` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): neither subsection mentions an accounting limited liability partnership
